{#- ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
    Turn Generation Prompt — split for prompt caching

    This template is rendered ONCE per turn and inserted as the **user**
    message.  The static instruction block now lives in the system message
    (assembled in ConversationGenerator._TURN_SYSTEM_PROMPT), so this file
    contains ONLY the variable, per-turn content: the persona, experience,
    conversation memory, current state, and any instant event.

    The system message (built in code) contains:
      • Role definition and character immersion instructions
      • All texting realism rules (no formatting, tone, shared language, etc.)
      • Message cadence definitions
      • Multi-message turn rules
      • Content & topic flow rules for all conversation styles
      • Coincidence budget and ending rules
      • Full output format specification (<turn> XML)

    This split maximises the byte-identical prefix across generation calls
    so that providers with automatic prompt caching can reuse the KV cache.
─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────── -#}
